! HCN <-> HNC intrinsic reaction coordinate, HF/STO-3G  (v0.86.0)
!
! TWO-STAGE test.  Stage 1 (run FIRST, from this tests/ directory):
!
!     ./studdft tests/test_v072_hcn_tsfreq.inp
!
! locates the HCN <-> HNC transition state with P-RFO and writes the
! TS Hessian file  test_v072_hcn_tsfreq_ts.hess  (geometry, energy,
! Cartesian Hessian, frequencies, normal modes).  Stage 2 -- THIS
! input -- follows the reaction path from that saddle with the
! Gonzalez-Schlegel second-order (GS2) predictor-corrector
! [C. Gonzalez, H.B. Schlegel, J. Chem. Phys. 90, 2154 (1989);
!  J. Phys. Chem. 94, 5523 (1990)].
!
! What to check (HF/STO-3G reference values, %irc_step 0.15,
! %irc_maxpoints 40):
!
!   * The stored TS is re-verified: E_TS = -91.564914657 Ha, exactly
!     one imaginary mode, nu = -1256.5 cm^-1 (the recomputed and the
!     stored frequency must agree); the "SCF at TS" line must report
!     consistency with the stored $energy to ~1e-11 Ha.
!   * REVERSE branch: monotonic descent over ~23 points to the HCN
!     minimum, last energy ~ -91.67520 Ha, i.e. ~69.2 kcal/mol below
!     the TS; the final frame of the trajectory file has C-H ~ 1.07 A,
!     C-N ~ 1.15 A, N...H ~ 2.2 A (linear HCN being approached).
!   * FORWARD branch: monotonic descent over ~29 points to the HNC
!     minimum, last energy ~ -91.64442 Ha (~49.9 kcal/mol below the
!     TS); final frame N-H ~ 1.01 A, C-N ~ 1.17 A.
!   * Each branch must terminate cleanly with either "minimum region
!     reached" (max Cartesian gradient below %irc_gtol) or "energy
!     increased (basin floor)" -- on the very flat tail of the HCN
!     valley the two are separated by ~1e-8 Ha, so OpenMP reduction
!     noise can select either; the endpoint energy is the same.  The
!     two trajectory files *_irc_forward.xyz / *_irc_reverse.xyz must
!     contain npoints+1 frames each (frame 0 = the TS).
!
! The energies above make the textbook profile: HNC lies ~19.3
! kcal/mol above HCN, the barrier from HCN is ~69 kcal/mol at this
! (deliberately crude) level of theory.
!
! The geometry block below only defines the atom list / basis
! assignment; the coordinates themselves are REPLACED by the TS
! geometry stored in the .hess file (a notice is printed).
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     irc
%charge  0
%mult    1
%read_hess test_v072_hcn_tsfreq_ts.hess
%irc_step      0.15
%irc_maxpoints 40
%irc_direction both
%geom angstrom
C   -0.55  -0.20   0.00
N    0.55  -0.20   0.00
H    0.00   0.95   0.00
*end
